From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AtomCode <noreply@atomgit.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Use native C++ static_assert without a macro wrapper

Modern libc++ uses static_assert expressions whose predicates contain
commas.  The legacy two-argument macro wrapper parses those commas as
additional macro arguments before the compiler can process the native
keyword.  Leave the C++11 keyword untouched when it is available.
---
 common/include/compiler-static_assert.h | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/common/include/compiler-static_assert.h b/common/include/compiler-static_assert.h
index a37160b..37fe0a3 100644
--- a/common/include/compiler-static_assert.h
+++ b/common/include/compiler-static_assert.h
@@ -10,7 +10,6 @@
 
 #if defined(DXX_HAVE_CXX11_STATIC_ASSERT)
 /* native */
-#define static_assert(C,M)	static_assert(C,M)
 #elif defined(DXX_HAVE_BOOST_STATIC_ASSERT)
 #include <boost/static_assert.hpp>
 #define static_assert(C,M)	BOOST_STATIC_ASSERT_MSG((C),M)
-- 
